From e445fd079052211eac047c313c86abaf72d6aed7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zswll2 <zswll2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 15:50:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/32] fix(desktop): reject split-shaped drag drops on
 touch/narrow + fold user splits

F4a: coarse-pointer or <=640px viewports now refuse split-shaped drops on
both drag paths (pane tabs via drag-session, sessions/tiles via
session-drag); stack/center drops are unchanged and denial keeps the
selection retryable. Drag-created splits persist SplitNode.origin:'user'
(written only by the two drag commit paths); entering a narrow viewport
folds user splits whose smaller column would fall below 280px by routing
the dropped column's panes through their existing close paths. The layout
reset gains a zone-menu row and 44px touch targets on the edit-bar card
for narrow reachability.
